---
import ContentLayout from '../../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: 'Website Audit', href: '/website-audit/' },
  { label: 'Content Audit', href: '/website-content-audit/' },
  { label: 'Content Audit Services', href: '/website-content-audit/services/' },
];

const toc = [
  { label: "What's Included", id: 'whats-included' },
  { label: 'When to Hire This Out', id: 'when-to-hire-this-out' },
  { label: 'Pricing', id: 'pricing' },
  { label: 'FAQ', id: 'faq' },
];

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  name: 'Content Audit Services',
  provider: { '@id': 'https://auditweb.site/#organization' },
  description: 'Done-for-you content audit services identifying thin, duplicate, and underperforming pages, with a prioritised action plan for each.',
  areaServed: ['US', 'GB'],
};
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Content Audit Services"
  description="Content audit services provide a scoped URL inventory, evidence-led page decisions and an implementation queue. AuditWeb packages start at USD 297."
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  toc={toc}
  schema={schema}
  showLeadForm={true}
  publishDate="2026-08-26"
  updateDate="2026-09-11"
>

<p>Content audit services combine a scoped URL inventory with page-level evidence and a practical implementation queue. AuditWeb assigns each reviewed page a keep, update, consolidate or remove decision and states data gaps where access or sampling limits the conclusion.</p>

<h2 id="whats-included">What's Included</h2>

  <p><strong>Scoped content inventory</strong> — intended canonical URLs catalogued from a crawl, sitemap and available platform exports. Relevant Search Console, analytics and link evidence is recorded with dates where access permits.</p>

<p><strong>Decision evidence</strong> — each reviewed page is assessed for current purpose, accuracy, task completion, search visibility, conversions, earned links, ownership and any legal or support need. A documented score can support triage but does not decide deletion or consolidation.</p>

<p><strong>Demand and answer gaps</strong> — unanswered customer tasks supported by query, business and competitor evidence. Each candidate records the source, confidence, expected value and production or maintenance cost rather than an opaque opportunity score.</p>

  <p><strong>Action plan</strong> — an ordered list marking reviewed pages as keep, update, consolidate or remove with evidence, dependencies and a success check. Traffic or revenue effects remain estimates until measured.</p>

<h2 id="when-to-hire-this-out">When to Hire This Out</h2>

  <p>External help is useful when the review scope exceeds internal capacity, a migration needs content decisions or a performance change needs independent diagnosis. Agree the URL set, data access, samples and deliverables before comparing proposals.</p>

<h2 id="pricing">Pricing</h2>

<div role="region" aria-label="Content audit service pricing" tabindex="0">
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Package</th>
      <th>Price</th>
      <th>Best For</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Focused audit</strong></td>
      <td>$297</td>
      <td>A confirmed priority section or URL sample</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Full audit</strong></td>
      <td>$997</td>
      <td>A confirmed site-wide review scope</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Custom audit</strong></td>
      <td>Custom</td>
      <td>Large, multi-site or specialist requirements agreed in the proposal</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<p>Page counts alone do not define effort. Rendering, language variants, data access and the depth of manual review can change the scope, so confirm the URL set and deliverables before purchase.</p>

<h2 id="faq">FAQ</h2>

<h3>Do you write the replacement content too?</h3>
<p>No. The audit covers diagnosis and a per-page action plan. Content writing is available as a separate engagement once the audit defines what needs writing.</p>

<h3>How long does a content audit take?</h3>
<p>The delivery date is agreed with the scope. It depends on the URL set, data access, rendering complexity and review depth; the proposal should state the date and any dependencies.</p>

<h3>What CMS access do you need?</h3>
<p>None required for the audit itself. Read-only Search Console and Analytics access lets us correlate content quality with actual performance data.</p>

</ContentLayout>
